\title{reactableEdit: Interactive and Editable Data Tables for R}
\description{
Interactive data tables for R, based on the 'React Table' JavaScript library. Provides an HTML widget that can be used in 'R Markdown' or 'Quarto' documents, 'Shiny' applications, or viewed from an R console. An independent fork of the 'reactable' package by Greg Lin, adding native 'Shiny' cell inputs with server validation, configurable disabled states, row addition and removal, and rich tooltips. Not an official release of the original 'reactable' project.
}
\details{
reactableEdit is an independent fork of \href{https://github.com/glin/reactable}{reactable},
originally developed by Greg Lin. It adds native Shiny cell editing with server
validation, configurable input states, row actions, and rich tooltips.
It is not an official release of the original project.

See the \href{https://github.com/samuel-jobert/reactableEdit}{fork repository} for
development and issue reports. The \href{https://glin.github.io/reactable/}{upstream documentation}
describes the shared API, but not the extensions in this fork.

Load the package with \code{library(reactableEdit)}. Function names such as
\code{reactable()} and \code{reactableOutput()}, the \code{Reactable} JavaScript API, widget
classes, and \verb{reactable.*} options retain their original names for compatibility.
The two packages can be installed alongside each other, but should not be
loaded together or have their widgets mixed in the same HTML document.
